<aura:documentation>
	<aura:description>
    <p>Card Attributes Component</p>

    <!-- LAST UPDATED DATE / VERSION -->
    <p>Last Updated: 4/30/2019</p>
    <p>CurrentVersion: 1.0</p>
    <hr/>
    <!-- UPDATE DATE / VERSION WITH ANY UPDATES -->
		<p>Structure of Card Attribute items:</p>
		<pre>
[
{
name: 'Competencies', // Section Title
types: [ // Links Entries separated by pipe if multiple`
 {
   id: '1',
   name: 'Competency 1', // link title`
   searchParams: '#Competency 1' // link url
 },
 {
   id: '2',
   name: 'Competency 2',
   searchParams: '#Competency 2'
 }
 ],
 // Optional
 cta: {
	 link: "#",
	 name: "Learn more about these designations"
 }
},
{	name: 'Geographical Regional Coverage',
	editButton: { // Optional for partner detail
		currentStep: '2'
	},
	typeGroupings: [
		{
			name: 'Asia-Pacific-Japan',
			types: [
				{
					id: '1',
					name: 'All Asia-Pacific-Japan Countries',
					searchParams: '#All Asia-Pacific-Japan Countries'
				}
			]
		},
		{
			name: 'Americas',
			types: [
				{
					id: '2',
					name: 'Canada',
					searchParams: 'Canada'
				},
				{
					id: '3',
					name: 'United States',
					searchParams: '#United States'
				},
				{
					id: '4',
					name: 'Mexico',
					searchParams: '#Mexico'
				}
			]
		},
	],
	cta: {
		"link": "#",
		"label" "Learn more about these designations"
	}
},
{
  name: 'Address', // Section Title
  textBlock: 'Pyramid Computer Gmbh Botzinger Strasse 60, D-79111 Freigburg,Germany' // Text block display accepts rich text
}

]
		</pre>
		<p>The card attribute items are displayed in order of the array. It currently accepts 2 different types of entries. The regular attribue entries separated by | or the textBlock type which can have a richtext data display.</p>
    <!-- CHANGELOG ADD ANY UPDATES HERE -->
    <hr/>
    <p>Change Log</p>
		<p>Added text block display option</p>

    <!-- CHANGELOG -->
  </aura:description>
</aura:documentation>